Why This Market Matters
IoT-enabled packaging creates a digital connection between physical products, manufacturers, supply-chain participants, retailers, and consumers. By combining packaging with identification technologies and connected sensors, companies can improve traceability, product authentication, inventory visibility, and customer interaction. Pharmaceutical and food applications can benefit from monitoring product conditions throughout distribution, while consumer brands can use connected packaging to provide product information and authentication. The integration of smart packaging with cloud platforms and analytics is also creating opportunities for data-driven supply-chain management.

